# ---- Verification scratch ----
# Falsification harnesses keep working copies here — `.bak` snapshots of
# install.sh, config.py, signing.py. Three separate reasons this must never be
# committed or shipped: the repository is public and a snapshot is a second copy
# of something whose single-copy-ness is the point; nothing on the server runs
# it; and a stale harness left behind can be executed against a newer tree,
# which clobbered this working tree twice during E2.2.
#
# Ignored here AND excluded from the tarball in both deploy scripts. The two are
# different holes: this one is `git add -A` on a public repo, that one is a
# package landing in /tmp on the server.
scratchpad/

# ---- Editors / OS ----
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
